        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "In this Section, the BN instances learned for each domain are presented. Each BN instance represents a single GEI domain and consists of input nodes coloured in orange, which always represent extra variables (see Section 4.2); GEI ingredients shown as white chance nodes, and a green output node representing the domain score, calculated using the official methodology. This involves taking an unweighted geometric mean of the sub-domain scores (when applicable), which are in turn the unweighted arithmetic mean of the ingredients involved. Figure 7 consists of five panels, each showing the estimated BN instance for a GEI domain, based on data available at the Italian provincial level.",
            "block_bbox": [
